      "summaries": {
        "en": "Tunnelto is a Rust-based tool that solves the common development challenge of exposing local web servers to the internet, eliminating complex network configuration. It works by creating secure tunnels through async I/O, efficiently forwarding traffic from a public URL to your localhost. Developers can use it to test webhooks, share prototypes, or collaborate remotely by simply running a command that generates an accessible endpoint for their local applications.",
        "zh": "Tunnelto 是一个基于 Rust 的工具，解决了开发中常见的将本地服务器暴露到互联网的难题，无需复杂网络配置。它通过异步 I/O 创建安全隧道，高效地将公共 URL 的流量转发到本地主机。开发者可以用它测试 Webhook、分享原型或远程协作，只需运行一条命令即可为本地应用生成可访问的端点，特别适合需要临时公开服务的开发调试场景。",
        "es": "Tunnelto is a Rust-based tool that solves the common development challenge of exposing local web servers to the internet, eliminating complex network configuration. It works by creating secure tunnels through async I/O, efficiently forwarding traffic from a public URL to your localhost. Developers can use it to test webhooks, share prototypes, or collaborate remotely by simply running a command that generates an accessible endpoint for their local applications.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "tunnelto stands out for async-io, expose, and localhost in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Tunnelto is a Rust-based tool that solves the common development challenge of exposing local web servers to the internet, eliminating complex network configuration. It works by creating secure tunnels through async I/O, efficiently forwarding traffic from a public URL to your localhost. Developers can use it to test webhooks, share prototypes, or collaborate remotely by simply running a command that generates an accessible endpoint for their local applications.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/agrinman/tunnelto for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
